specific adjustment must be explicit."],"condition":"H.R. 2021 of the 119th Congress does not become law on or before 2027-01-14T23:59:59Z.","id":"not_enacted","label":"American Teacher Act not enacted"}],"condition_deadline":"2027-01-14T23:59:59Z","condition_resolution_note":"No condition resolver is registered. The proposed rule requires the exact H.R. 2021 (119th Congress) official enacted-law association plus a dated BecameLaw action, cross-checked against the law publication. Another legislative vehicle, S. 2481 or a later Congress does not satisfy this identity. After cutoff, absence of enactment needs a fresh complete official record. Missing, contradictory or boundary-day evidence lacking sufficient timestamp precision stays unresolved. January 14 is a chosen scenario cutoff, not a claimed constitutional last-presentment date.","exhaustive":true,"limitations":["Exploratory local-operator forecasts; neither prospective registration nor calibrated causal policy-effect estimates.","No automatic condition or numeric-outcome resolver is registered. These scenarios cannot enter ranks or training rewards.","NCES estimates a Fall 2030 release but has not supplied an exact day. Historical API means are current-vintage captures, not authenticated original-release prints.","Enactment can occur with amendments; the forecast assumes the introduced grant mechanism materially survives. Funding and implementation are modeled assumptions.","Public-school effects need not generalize to the full NT population. Indonesia and district-level Texas evidence do not identify a national U.S. NAEP effect.","The difference between marginal conditional forecast medians has no identified causal interpretation or uncertainty interval without a joint model."],"methodology":"paired_conditional_v1","outcome":{"country":"US","geography":"Nation (NT)","measure":"Main NAEP mathematics MRPCM composite; TOTAL; MN:MN mean on the 0-500 scale","measurement_period":"2030","name":"2030 NAEP grade 8 mathematics national mean","population":"All students, public and nonpublic schools, grade 8; R3 accommodations permitted","release_date":null,"resolution_rule":"Proposed outcome: the first official NCES release reporting the 2030 main NAEP grade 8 mathematics national NT, TOTAL, MRPCM, R3 mean, using its publisher whole-number score. Do not substitute national-public NP, later revisions, a different framework target, or an inferred rounding tie rule. No automatic outcome resolver is registered; schedule or definition changes remain explicit barriers to admission.","resolution_source_url":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/reports/mathematics/","unit":"NAEP points"},"question":"What will the 2030 national NAEP grade 8 mathematics score be if the American Teacher Act becomes law, and if it does not?","reference_description":"One common predictive starting distribution from the frozen NT history, persistence and explicit common recovery/trend assumptions. This reference is not a probability-weighted unconditional mixture of the two arms.","schema_version":"thesis_conditional_contract_v1","scoring_status":"not_registered","shared_evidence":[{"claim":"The exact population is National NT, all students including public and nonpublic schools; mathematics MRPCM composite, grade 8, TOTAL, MN:MN, R3 accommodations permitted. NP is a different public-only population.","source_ids":["naep-api","naep-population"]},{"claim":"The shared history contains current official API unrounded means. The target is the publisher whole-number mean; 2019, 2022 and 2024 published NT anchors are 282, 274 and 274. These captures do not prove the historical first print. Do not substitute NP values.","source_ids":["naep-history","naep-summary","naep-reporting"]},{"claim":"NCES estimates Winter 2030 assessment and Fall 2030 report release; there is no verified exact publication day. A framework update starts in 2026. Treat comparability, cohort recovery and irregular assessment intervals explicitly, without assuming independent annual changes.","source_ids":["naep-calendar","naep-framework"]},{"claim":"H.R. 2021 was introduced March 10, 2025 and referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce. The official status XML captured September 7, 2026 contains no enacted-law record. This describes the captured state, not the future condition result.","source_ids":["hr2021-status"]},{"claim":"Introduced H.R. 2021 section 3 proposes four-year state grants for a $60,000 teacher salary floor for school year 2026-27 with inflation adjustment. State applications and sustainability assurances are required; at least 85% goes to local-agency subgrants, with Title I and rural priorities. Qualifying schools are public elementary/secondary schools. Section 8 authorizes such sums as necessary for FY2026-30; it does not appropriate a fixed funding amount.","source_ids":["hr2021-text"]},{"claim":"H.R. 2021 section 3(c) requires grants to supplement and not supplant other Federal, State and local public funds for teacher base salaries; prohibits reducing or adjusting teacher pay or state teacher loan forgiveness due to grant eligibility; and requires the same state/local compensation funds for each teacher and school as absent the Act. Do not treat simple replacement of planned state/local teacher compensation spending as permitted implementation. Any crowd-out rationale must distinguish prohibited noncompliance or weak enforcement from a separately explained indirect fiscal adjustment consistent with these rules.","source_ids":["hr2021-text"]},{"claim":"J-PAL describes a randomized acceleration of salary doubling for eligible incumbent teachers in Indonesia: 120 treatment schools and 240 controls, 360 total. No detectable student test-score improvement after 2-3 years was reported. This is not proof of exactly zero effect, and no direct conversion to U.S. national NAEP points follows.","source_ids":["jpal-indonesia"]},{"claim":"Hendricks estimates a Texas salary-turnover elasticity of -1.4. His retention-only simulation of a 5% salary increase projects average teacher value-added gains of 0.0005 SD within 3 years and 0.0007 SD within 10 years. These are modeled teacher-productivity changes, not observed national NAEP gains. Turnover includes district moves. Do not linearly scale these figures to a large nationwide salary floor or treat district recruitment gains as national net gains.","source_ids":["hendricks-texas"]}],"shared_history":[{"period":"2003","source_id":"naep-history","value":277.563392032194},{"period":"2005","source_id":"naep-history","value":278.819811032215},{"period":"2007","source_id":"naep-history","value":281.34568687101},{"period":"2009","source_id":"naep-history","value":282.909818195293},{"period":"2011","source_id":"naep-history","value":283.851219074008},{"period":"2013","source_id":"naep-history","value":284.606823544421},{"period":"2015","source_id":"naep-history","value":282.221908868416},{"period":"2017","source_id":"naep-history","value":282.842676160565},{"period":"2019","source_id":"naep-history","value":282.001859415618},{"period":"2022","source_id":"naep-history","value":274.266213337059},{"period":"2024","source_id":"naep-history","value":273.833456014299}],"sources":[{"artifact":{"bytes":7932,"media_type":"application/json","sha256":"50d5193160023a4db07b4926d29a99513953ac1d8924ee3405e4f30158dfc3b1"},"id":"naep-history","retrieved_at":"2026-09-07T10:33:44.234278Z","title":"NCES NAEP official historical means","url":"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/DataService/GetAdhocData.aspx?type=data&subject=mathematics&grade=8&subscale=MRPCM&variable=TOTAL&jurisdiction=NT,NP&stattype=MN%3AMN&Year=2024,2022,2019,2017,2015,2013,2011,2009,2007,2005,2003&Program=NDE"},{"artifact":{"bytes":12355,"media_type":"text/html","sha256":"5b16b3dba81754eaff7984e5c35149417f28cdbece385ef7dfe919bfc81d665c"},"id":"naep-population","retrieved_at":"2026-09-07T10:33:44.234218Z","title":"NCES national and national-public jurisdicti